WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:08.458
<v Audio Description>Visual scene one: Card one lights up amber while glowing cyan bit switches flip across a dark 3D silicon die above an amber joule counter.

2
00:00:08.798 --> 00:00:15.300
<v Presenter>First, every calculation is a physical event where flipping silicon switches spends real energy in joules.

3
00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:25.314
<v Audio Description>Visual scene two: Card two glows cyan as the board separates physical wire-shunt traces from chip counters and drops flat to zero clock pulses between jobs.

4
00:00:25.654 --> 00:00:32.914
<v Presenter>Second, honest hardware audits separate wire current sensors from chip counters, while sleeping between real jobs.

5
00:00:33.254 --> 00:00:42.835
<v Audio Description>Visual scene three: Card three turns emerald as single-cycle Boolean lookup cubes replace tall, hot decimal arithmetic blocks at a twentyfold compile cut.

6
00:00:43.175 --> 00:00:50.691
<v Presenter>Third, single-cycle Boolean lookup circuits replace heavy decimal arithmetic on repeated checks with tiny hardware steps.
